      "id": "za3d7xp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Time Period of the Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Age is broadly divided into the Early Vedic Period (1500–1000 BCE) and the Later Vedic Period (1000–500 BCE).",
        "The four sacred canonical texts are the Rigveda, Samaveda, Yajurveda, and Atharvaveda.",
        "Society evolved from tribal pastoralism in the Early Vedic age to settled agriculture and territorial states in the Later Vedic age.",
        "Democratic political assemblies like the Sabha, Samiti, Vidatha, and Gana held significant influence during the Early Vedic period.",
        "Religion shifted from atmospheric nature worship centered around Indra and Agni to ritualistic worship centered around Prajapati, Vishnu, and Rudra."
      ],
      "id": "7saz6tp"
    },
